 "caveats": "Segments are the earliest point an encounter is reachable, judged from HM badges (Rock Smash after Coal, Cut after Forest, Defog after Fen, Surf after Relic = 5 badges, Strength after Mine, Rock Climb after Icicle, Waterfall after Beacon), the Bicycle after the Galactic Eterna Building, the Good Rod on Route 209 and the Super Rod in the post-game Fight Area. Swarms, the Poké Radar, dual-slot GBA encounters, Trophy Garden, anything needing the National Dex, the other fossils, Rotom, Eevee, Snowpoint Temple, Stark Mountain, the Battle Zone routes and Giratina (Turnback Cave) all count as post-game; Great Marsh slots tagged as daily count from Pastoria unless they need the National Dex. Dialga (Diamond) / Palkia (Pearl), Uxie, Azelf and roaming Mesprit come after Spear Pillar, before Volkner. The Skull (Cranidos) and Armor (Shieldon) fossils from the Underground are version-split before the National Dex, but are shown in both versions. Mt. Coronet floors, Lake Valor and the Victory Road side passages are assigned by area and are approximate; evolutions are shown from the base form's segment regardless of level, stone or trade requirements."
